## Data: what you may do

- **Browse and search** the roster on <https://vietprofs.roars.dev>.
- **Cite or mention individual facts** (for example a person's name,
  university, and department) in an article, a personal reference, an
  academic citation, or a conversation.
- **Link** to the site or to individual profile pages.

## Data: what needs written permission

Without a separate written license from the copyright holder, you may not:

- copy, download, scrape, crawl, or otherwise extract the roster, or any
  substantial part of it, by automated or manual means;
- redistribute, republish, or mirror the roster or any substantial part of
  it, whether complete, filtered, re-sorted, merged, or otherwise modified;
- use the roster, or anything built from it, in any AI/ML training or
  evaluation corpus, or in any commercial product or service (including
  paid services, advertising-supported platforms, lead generation, or
  recruiting).

Nothing in this license restricts uses that copyright law recognizes as
already free regardless of license terms.

Copies of the data obtained earlier under the CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 license keep
that license's terms; this license governs the data from 2026-10-11 onward.

## Excluded material

**Portraits** (`public/portraits/`) are sourced from official university
pages and personal/lab sites, used here for identification purposes; they
remain the property of their original sources and are not covered by this
license. The manuscript (`paper.tex`/`paper.pdf`) is also not covered by
this license.

For permission beyond this license's scope (bulk access to the data,
commercial use, a derivative version of the code), email root@roars.dev.
